Mark Landsman, Filmmaker of SCANDALOUS: The Untold Story of the National Enquirer:
...And that's not to say that like I was
born to make a story about a supermarket

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:06.359
tabloid. Like I never read The Enquirer
growing up, I never cared about

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.340
supermarket tabloids. I thought it was a
joke.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.960
Film Courage: I was listening to an interview with
John Pilger he's a journalist and

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.850
someone in the audience yelled out at a
Q&amp; A "There's this issue..."

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:23.450
and went on and on "What are you doing
about it." Because he covers various

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:27.320
issues in his films and he said [Paraphrasing] "Well why
do I have to be the poster child of

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:31.910
having to do something about it. We can
all do something about it nowadays." how

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.390
do you feel about that because it used
